@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix foundation: <http://foundation.local/ontology/> .

<http://foundation.local/ontology/Plans_20260302_105354>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <http://foundation.local/ontology/Plan> ,
                <http://foundation.local/ontology/SoftwareFeature> ,
                <http://foundation.local/ontology/UserStory> ,
                <http://foundation.local/ontology/Persona> .

# =============================================================================
# Feature: Ontology Export via App Menu
# =============================================================================

foundation:Feature_20260302_105354 a foundation:SoftwareFeature ;
    rdfs:label "Ontology Export via App Menu" ;
    foundation:overview """
Allow the user to export their ontology (classes and properties) as TTL files to a
folder of their choice, triggered from the native app menu bar. The export groups
definitions by their origin file, generating one TTL file per source file (plus a
user-defined.ttl for items created via the UI). This enables backup, sharing, and
use in external ontology tools.
""" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending .

# --- Persona ---

foundation:Persona_20260302_105354_knowledge_worker a foundation:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge Worker" ;
    foundation:personaGoals """
Manage and share structured knowledge. Uses the app to build domain ontologies and
wants to export them for backup, version control, or use in other tools (e.g.
Protégé, SPARQL endpoints).
""" ;
    foundation:personaContext """
Desktop user, macOS. Intermediate familiarity with ontologies and TTL format.
Uses the app regularly to define classes and properties. Expects the export to work
like any native macOS "Export..." menu item.
""" .

# --- User Story ---

foundation:UserStory_20260302_105354_export_ontology a foundation:UserStory ;
    rdfs:label "As a knowledge worker, I want to export my ontology as TTL files" ;
    foundation:userRole foundation:Persona_20260302_105354_knowledge_worker ;
    foundation:capability "export all ontology classes and properties to TTL files in a folder of my choice" ;
    foundation:benefit "I can back up, share, or use my ontology definitions in external tools" ;
    foundation:acceptanceCriteria """
- The app menu bar contains a "File" menu with an "Export Ontology..." item
- Clicking "Export Ontology..." opens a native folder-picker dialog
- After selecting a folder, TTL files are written there grouped by source file
  (e.g. Task.ttl, Status.ttl, user-defined.ttl)
- Each exported TTL file contains: @prefix declarations, owl:Ontology header,
  all class definitions (rdf:type, rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:subClassOf),
  and all property definitions (rdf:type, rdfs:label, rdfs:domain, rdfs:range)
  that originated from that source
- Classes and properties from RDF/RDFS/OWL built-ins are excluded
- A native OS notification (or log entry) informs the user of success or failure
- If the user cancels the folder picker, nothing happens
""" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:partOfFeature foundation:Feature_20260302_105354 .

# --- Plans ---

foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 a foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan ;
    rdfs:label "Ontology Export — Backend" ;
    foundation:plannedAt "2026-03-02T10:53:54"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:overview """
All export logic lives in Rust/Tauri backend. No frontend changes are required.

1. Add tauri-plugin-dialog dependency for the native folder-picker dialog.
2. Create src-tauri/src/commands/ontology.rs with:
   - ontology__export(executor, folder_path): queries classes and properties from
     the database, groups by origin file, serializes to TTL, writes files to disk.
   - serialize_group_to_ttl(groups): builds TTL string with @prefix block, owl:Ontology
     header, class blocks, and property blocks.
3. Register the command in lib.rs invoke_handler and mod.rs.
4. In lib.rs setup(), build a native menu with a "File" submenu containing
   "Export Ontology..." (id = "export-ontology").
5. In on_menu_event, handle "export-ontology": open folder dialog via
   app.dialog().file().pick_folder(), then call the export logic using DbExecutor
   from app state (app.state::<DbExecutor>()).
6. Notify success/error via tauri::notification or log entry.

Query strategy:
- Join triples (rdf:type owl:Class / owl:ObjectProperty / owl:DatatypeProperty)
  with their origin_id → origins.name to determine source file.
- Join origins.name with ontology_files.file_name to obtain the TTL file name.
- Exclude subjects whose IRI starts with rdf:, rdfs:, owl:, xsd: (built-ins).
- For each subject, collect ALL its non-retracted triples to reconstruct the full
  definition.
- Group definitions by file_name; unrecognised origins go into user-defined.ttl.
""" ;
    foundation:risks """
- tauri-plugin-dialog is not currently installed; add it to Cargo.toml and lib.rs.
- DbExecutor may not be registered yet if initialize_app has not been called;
  guard against this with a graceful error message.
- The link between triples.origin_id and ontology_files may be indirect (via
  origins.name == ontology_files.file_name); verify the join at implementation time.
- rio_turtle crate supports reading but not writing; use a hand-written TTL
  serializer (straightforward given the well-known structure).
- Large ontologies with many triples could be slow; run export on a blocking
  thread via tokio::task::spawn_blocking.
""" ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:UserStory_20260302_105354_export_ontology .

# =============================================================================
# Tasks
# =============================================================================

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_add_dialog_plugin a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Add tauri-plugin-dialog dependency" ;
    foundation:description """
In src-tauri/Cargo.toml, add:
  tauri-plugin-dialog = "2"

In src-tauri/src/lib.rs, in the Builder chain, add:
  .plugin(tauri_plugin_dialog::init())

This enables app.dialog().file().pick_folder() in the menu event handler.
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/Cargo.toml, src-tauri/src/lib.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_create_export_module a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Create ontology export command module" ;
    foundation:description """
Create src-tauri/src/commands/ontology.rs.

Expose one public async command:
  pub async fn ontology__export(
      executor: State<'_, DbExecutor>,
      folder_path: String,
  ) -> Result<String, String>

Logic:
1. executor.read(|conn| { /* queries */ }).await — collect classes and properties:
   a. Classes: SELECT t.subject, t.origin_id, origins.name as origin_name, of.file_name, ...
      FROM triples t
      JOIN origins ON origins.id = t.origin_id
      LEFT JOIN ontology_files of ON of.file_name = origins.name
      WHERE t.predicate = 'rdf:type' AND t.object = 'owl:Class' AND t.retracted = 0
        AND t.subject NOT LIKE 'rdf:%' AND t.subject NOT LIKE 'rdfs:%'
        AND t.subject NOT LIKE 'owl:%' AND t.subject NOT LIKE 'xsd:%'
   b. Properties: same join pattern but object IN ('owl:ObjectProperty',
      'owl:DatatypeProperty', 'owl:AnnotationProperty')
   c. For each collected subject IRI, fetch all its non-retracted triples:
      SELECT predicate, object, object_value, object_type, object_datatype
      FROM triples WHERE subject = ? AND retracted = 0

2. Group subjects by COALESCE(file_name, 'user-defined') as output_file_name.

3. For each group, call serialize_group_to_ttl() and write to
   Path::new(&folder_path).join(output_file_name).

4. Return a summary string: "Exported N files to <folder_path>".
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/src/commands/ontology.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_add_dialog_plugin ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_create_ttl_serializer a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Implement TTL serializer helper" ;
    foundation:description """
Add a private fn serialize_group_to_ttl(subjects: &[SubjectTriples], ontology_iri: &str) -> String
inside src-tauri/src/commands/ontology.rs.

Output format:
  @prefix rdf:        <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
  @prefix rdfs:       <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
  @prefix owl:        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
  @prefix xsd:        <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
  @prefix foundation: <http://foundation.local/ontology/> .

  <http://foundation.local/ontology/{ontology_iri}>
      a owl:Ontology .

  foundation:MyClass a owl:Class ;
      rdfs:label "My Class" ;
      rdfs:comment "..." ;
      rdfs:subClassOf foundation:Parent .

Use namespaces::compress_iri() (already in src-tauri/src/namespaces.rs) to shorten
full IRIs. Escape literal values that contain quotes or newlines.
The function returns a UTF-8 string; the caller writes it to disk with std::fs::write().
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/src/commands/ontology.rs, src-tauri/src/namespaces.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_create_export_module ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_register_command a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Register ontology__export command in mod.rs and lib.rs" ;
    foundation:description """
In src-tauri/src/commands/mod.rs:
  mod ontology;
  pub use ontology::*;

In src-tauri/src/lib.rs, inside tauri::generate_handler![...], add:
  commands::ontology__export,
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/src/commands/mod.rs, src-tauri/src/lib.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_create_ttl_serializer ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_add_menu a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Build native app menu in lib.rs setup()" ;
    foundation:description """
In src-tauri/src/lib.rs, inside the .setup(|app| { ... }) closure, construct a menu:

  use tauri::menu::{MenuBuilder, SubmenuBuilder, MenuItem};

  let export_item = MenuItem::with_id(app, "export-ontology", "Export Ontology...", true, None::<&str>)?;
  let file_menu = SubmenuBuilder::new(app, "File")
      .item(&export_item)
      .build()?;
  let menu = MenuBuilder::new(app)
      .item(&file_menu)
      .build()?;
  app.set_menu(menu)?;

This creates the native macOS menu bar with File > Export Ontology...
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/src/lib.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_register_command ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_handle_menu_event a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Implement on_menu_event handler for export action" ;
    foundation:description """
Directly after building the menu in setup(), register the event handler:

  let app_handle = app.handle().clone();
  app.on_menu_event(move |_app, event| {
      if event.id() == "export-ontology" {
          let handle = app_handle.clone();
          tauri::async_runtime::spawn(async move {
              use tauri_plugin_dialog::DialogExt;
              handle.dialog()
                  .file()
                  .pick_folder(move |folder_path| {
                      if let Some(path) = folder_path {
                          let handle2 = handle.clone();
                          tauri::async_runtime::spawn(async move {
                              let executor = handle2.state::<crate::eavto::executor::DbExecutor>();
                              match crate::commands::ontology__export(executor, path.to_string_lossy().to_string()).await {
                                  Ok(msg) => log::info!("Ontology export: {}", msg),
                                  Err(err) => log::error!("Ontology export failed: {}", err),
                              }
                          });
                      }
                  });
          });
      }
  });

Note: DbExecutor is available via app.state() only after initialize_app has been called.
Guard with try_state() and surface a user-visible error if not ready.
""" ;
    foundation:notes "src-tauri/src/lib.rs" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_add_menu ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .

foundation:Task_20260302_105354_verify a foundation:Task ;
    rdfs:label "Verify ontology export with cargo check" ;
    foundation:description """
Run: cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml

Confirm:
- No compilation errors in ontology.rs, lib.rs, commands/mod.rs
- tauri-plugin-dialog resolves correctly
- All menu API types compile
- ontology__export signature matches the invoke_handler registration

Then manually test in dev mode:
- App menu shows "File > Export Ontology..."
- Clicking opens a folder picker
- After selecting, TTL files appear in the folder grouped by source
- Files contain valid Turtle syntax (validate with rapper or Protégé)
""" ;
    foundation:hasStatus foundation:Pending ;
    foundation:dependsOn foundation:Task_20260302_105354_handle_menu_event ;
    foundation:contributesTo foundation:BackendArchitecturePlan_20260302_105354 .
